<title>USA: Nomura Securities to lose legal officer - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Nomura Securities to lose legal officer - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ira Lee Sorkin, hired by Nomura Securities International Inc in May 1995 to beef up the securities firm's legal and compliance group, will resign, The Wall Street Journal reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>The planned resignation of the chief legal officer is to be announced Tuesday, the story said.</p>
<p>It comes a few months after the U.S. unit of Japan's giant Nomura Securities Co hired William Maitland from Merrill Lynch &amp; Co as general counsel, the story says.</p>
</text>
